  "dom_id": "step-q128382",
  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given the Cartesian equation $3x+5y+15=0$ of the plane $\u03a0$, find an equation of $\u03a0$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $\u03a0$ is $n=\u27e83,5,0\u27e9.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $\u03a0$ for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+5y+15 & =0 \\\\ 5y & =-3x-15 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{3}{5}x-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put, say, $x=0$, we get $y=-3.$ Hence, the point $P(0,-3,0)$ lies on $\u03a0.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=\u27e80,-3,0\u27e9.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-\u27e80,-3,0\u27e9)\\cdot \u27e83,5,0\u27e9 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
